Retraction Watch Database
https://gitlab.com/crossref/retraction-watch-data
Collected by Retraction Watch (The Center for Scientific Integrity);
distributed by Crossref.

  engine/src/co_scientist/platform/retrieval/data/retractions.txt.gz

    A derived extract, not a copy: only the retraction and original-paper
    DOI of every row whose RetractionNature is "Retraction", normalized,
    deduplicated and sorted -- none of the dataset's other columns
    (titles, authors, institutions, reasons) are retained or shipped.
    Rebuilt from the upstream CSV by app/dev/refresh_retractions.py; the
    extract committed here was generated 2026-09-24.

    Used by engine/src/co_scientist/platform/retrieval/retraction_set.py as a second, independent retraction
    check in engine/src/co_scientist/platform/retrieval/citations, alongside whatever the source
    (PubMed/OpenAlex) already flags -- retraction propagation between
    indexes can lag by months.

    Neither Crossref's documentation nor the upstream repository states a
    licence for this data; Crossref describes it only as "publicly
    available". Shipping bare DOIs rather than the dataset is a
    deliberate response to that silence: a DOI is a factual identifier,
    and the dataset's expressive content -- its titles, reasons,
    authors and institutions -- is what we do not redistribute. Anyone
    extending this to carry more than identifiers should settle the
    terms with Crossref first.
